rent weather\n    weather_url = \"https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast\"\n    params = {\n        \"latitude\": lat,\n        \"longitude\": lon,\n        \"current\": \"temperature_2m,relative_humidity_2m,apparent_temperature,\"\n                   \"weather_code,wind_speed_10m\",\n    }\n    resp = requests.get(weather_url, params=params, timeout=10)\n    resp.raise_for_status()\n    return resp.json()[\"current\"]\n\ndef main():\n    city = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"Antwerp\"\n    try:\n        current = get_weather(city)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    print(f\"Weather in {city}:\")\n    print(f\"  Condition:   {WEATHER_CODES.get(current['weather_code'], 'Unknown')}\")\n    print(f\"  Temperature: {current['temperature_2m']}°C\")\n    print(f\"  Feels like:  {current['apparent_temperature']}°C\")\n    print(f\"  Humidity:    {current['relative_humidity_2m']}%\")\n    print(f\"  Wind speed:  {current['wind_speed_10m']} km/h\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```bash\npip install requests\npython weather.py \"Antwerp\"\n```\n\n**Example output:**\n\n```\nWeather in Antwerp:\n  Condition:   Partly cloudy\n  Temperature: 14.2°C\n  Feels like:  13.0°C\n  Humidity:    76%\n  Wind speed:  12.5 km/h\n```\n\n**Notes:**\n- Open-Meteo is free for non-commercial use with no API key needed.\n- If you prefer **OpenWeatherMap**, you'd register for a free key and call `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q={city}&appid={YOUR_KEY}` instead — happy to write that variant if you'd like.\n- The script includes timeouts and error handling so it fails gracefully on network issues or unknown cities.", "turn_1_finish_reason": "stop", "prompt_tokens": 575, "completion_tokens": 1001, "total_tokens": 1576, "tok_s": 93.55, "engine_generation_tps": null, "engine_prompt_tps": null, "engine_peak_memory_gb": null, "turn_2_elapsed_s": null, "turn_2_tool_calls": null, "turn_2_text